<title>ITALY: Milan to replace Turin as Alitalia cargo hub.</title>
<headline>Milan to replace Turin as Alitalia cargo hub.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alitalia  said it will cease using Turin's Caselle airport as its north Italian cargo hub with effect from December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>During the next six months, all of its cargo activities at Turin will be gradually switched to Milan-Malpensa, which will become the new northern hub, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>The airline had a total of 466 all-cargo flights to/from Turin using both Boeing 747 and McDonell Douglas DC-10 freighters in 1996, it said.</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017 --www.racs.com</p>
